  "alt": "An application can send rerank requests two ways. One path goes over the network to a hosted API such as Cohere Rerank, with no infrastructure to run but a network hop and a fee per request. The other goes to an open-source model such as bge-reranker-large running locally on the team's own GPU, with no network hop but a fixed infrastructure cost.",
  "caption": "A hosted API trades a network hop and per-call fees for zero infrastructure; a local model trades a GPU for neither.",
